# Query hooks in apps/web

Call `useQuery`, `useMutation`, `useInfiniteQuery`, and `useSuspenseQuery` only in custom hooks under `apps/web/app/queries/hooks/`. One exported hook per file; the filename matches the hook (`useGardens.ts` exports `useGardens`).

Keep keys, `queryOptions`, and `api()` wrappers in `app/queries/*`. Hooks wrap those factories. Loaders may still `queryClient.query(*Query())` — that is not a React hook.

Pages call the custom hooks and pass results into organisms. Never import TanStack Query data hooks in routes or `app/components/`. `useQueryClient` used for cache writes lives in the mutation hook.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Put each hook in `app/queries/hooks/useSomething.ts` (or `.tsx` if the hook renders JSX)
- Wrap `useQuery(gardensQuery())` in `useGardens`, `useMutation` in `useCreateGarden`, and so on
- Call those hooks from pages; pass `data` / callbacks as props

**Don't**

- Call `useQuery` / `useMutation` in a route, atom, molecule, organism, or template
- Export more than one hook from a file
- Put `queryOptions` or `api()` wrappers inside the hook file
- Use `useQueryClient` in a page to patch cache after a mutation

## Good / bad

```tsx
// apps/web/app/queries/hooks/useGardens.ts
export function useGardens() {
  return useQuery(gardensQuery());
}

// apps/web/app/routes/gardens-index.tsx
const { data, isPending, isError, refetch } = useGardens();
```

```tsx
// Bad — data hook in a page or component
export default function GardensIndexPage() {
  const { data } = useQuery(gardensQuery());
}
```
